                method: 'A gradient-boosting classifier (scikit-learn HistGradientBoosting) scores every regular-season shot since 1996-97 (5.93 million) from its court location, distance, angle, zone, two or three, period, seconds left in the period and season. Shot quality is the expected eFG% of a player\'s own shots; shot-making is his actual eFG% minus that, with a binomial 95% range; points above expected is the same gap in points. Every player is scored by a model trained on the other four-fifths of players (5 folds), so his own makes never raise the bar he is measured against. Seasons under 200 attempts are shown but not ranked. The Quality map tab reuses the same cross-fitted predictions: every shot with a recorded location is binned into 2.08-foot hexagons of the half court, and per player-season (200+ attempts) and per league season each cell keeps its attempts, makes and expected makes; a cell is coloured by the player\'s FG% there minus either the expected FG% (the model) or the league\'s FG% from the same hexagon that season, shrunk toward zero as if 5 more shots had gone in at the reference rate so a one-shot cell can\'t look extreme (the hover shows the raw counts). Shot value (round 6 step 8, Shot Charts › Shot value; scripts/build_shot_value.py, model in scripts/shot_value_lib.py): every regular-season attempt from 2020-21 on is priced before its game twice. Average shooter: the same boosting model, but fitted only on the seasons before the priced one (and on none of the shooter\'s fifth of players: 30 fits), moved by the league\'s level so far that season (the shrunk running log-odds gap of every earlier attempt, so opening night is unmoved); a free throw at last season\'s league rate, moved the same way. This shooter: the same plus his skill on the log-odds scale as of the day before, one number for each of four kinds of attempt (at the rim, other twos, threes, free throws). Skill is a hidden state: it starts at his NBA debut near a rookie\'s average, keeps a share of itself from one season to the next and gains some drift, and every game\'s attempts update it (a Laplace step from the current value), so no attempt\'s price uses its own game or a later one. The four settings per kind (rookie start and spread, carry-over, drift) were estimated by empirical Bayes, the likelihood of every attempt of 2010-11 to 2019-20, before any priced season: rim a rookie starts 2.4 points under average (±4.8), carry-over 0.82, drift ±2.8 a season, established players spread ±4.8; other twos −3.4 (±4.2), 0.90, ±1.7, ±3.8; threes −2.1 (±3.4), 0.94, ±0.9, ±2.6; free throws −2.1 (±6.6), 0.96, ±2.7, ±8.6 (percentage points at the 2025-26 league rate). Skill points = this shooter minus the average shooter (what his record said his shooting adds); beyond = points scored minus this shooter\'s price (what he made past that this season, luck included); Shot Value Added = skill points on field goals and free throws.',
